<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anton Korošec</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1872–1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anton Korošec was a Slovene Catholic priest and politician who presided over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-slovenes-croats-and-serbs">State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs</a> proclaimed in October 1918. He led the Slovene People's Party for two decades and served in many governments of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, becoming its only non-Serb prime minister in 1928 to 1929.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anton-korosec.jpg" alt="Anton Korošec" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: o.Ang. · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-2010-0420-501,_Anton_Korosec.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
